From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Thu, 29 Oct 2026 15:51:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] soc/intel/cannonlake: Add options for SpeedStep and Turbo
 Boost

Enhanced Intel SpeedStep and Turbo Boost come from the devicetree only
(eist_enable, cpu_turbo_disable). Let the option backend change them,
with the names the Haswell CPU code reads ("eist", "turbo_mode"):

- "eist" sets EIST in IA32_MISC_ENABLE and decides whether the SSDT
  gets the P-state tables, defaulting to eist_enable;
- "turbo_mode" off disables Turbo Boost; on, the devicetree still can
  (cpu_turbo_disable).

Without the options set nothing changes.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TnH4v9ZgSCT6oudGt6KtJL
---
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c | 5 +++--
 src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c  | 8 +++++---
 2 files changed, 8 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c
index 23918eeee2..002293f67a 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/acpi.c
@@ -12,6 +12,7 @@
 #include <intelblocks/pmclib.h>
 #include <intelblocks/acpi.h>
 #include <intelblocks/p2sb.h>
+#include <option.h>
 #include <soc/cpu.h>
 #include <soc/iomap.h>
 #include <soc/nvs.h>
@@ -142,8 +143,8 @@ void soc_power_states_generation(int core_id, int cores_per_package)
 {
 	config_t *config = config_of_soc();
 
-	/* Generate P-state tables */
-	if (config->eist_enable)
+	/* Generate P-state tables, with EIST on (cpu.c) */
+	if (get_uint_option("eist", config->eist_enable))
 		generate_p_state_entries(core_id, cores_per_package);
 }
 
diff --git a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c
index 888db5cdff..52b5e7ee96 100644
--- a/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c
+++ b/src/soc/intel/cannonlake/cpu.c
@@ -8,6 +8,7 @@
 #include <cpu/intel/turbo.h>
 #include <intelblocks/cpulib.h>
 #include <intelblocks/mp_init.h>
+#include <option.h>
 #include <soc/cpu.h>
 #include <soc/msr.h>
 #include <soc/pci_devs.h>
@@ -53,8 +54,8 @@ static void configure_misc(void)
 	msr.lo |= (1 << 3);	/* TM1/TM2/EMTTM enable */
 	wrmsr(IA32_MISC_ENABLE, msr);
 
-	/* Set EIST status */
-	cpu_set_eist(conf->eist_enable);
+	/* Set EIST status: the "eist" option, or the devicetree without it */
+	cpu_set_eist(get_uint_option("eist", conf->eist_enable));
 
 	/* Disable Thermal interrupts */
 	msr.lo = 0;
@@ -145,7 +146,8 @@ void soc_core_init(struct device *cpu)
 	/* Set energy policy */
 	set_energy_perf_bias(ENERGY_POLICY_NORMAL);
 
-	if (cfg->cpu_turbo_disable)
+	/* The "turbo_mode" option can turn off what the devicetree enables */
+	if (cfg->cpu_turbo_disable || !get_uint_option("turbo_mode", 1))
 		disable_turbo();
 	else
 		enable_turbo();
-- 
